From: Yanghan Ye <yyh94306@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 4 Aug 2026 13:20:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] netfilter: flowtable: tear down stale XFRM hardware flows

The software flowtable path validates cached XFRM destinations before every
packet, but packets handled by a hardware flow never reach that check.  An
XFRM state can therefore remain programmed after it has been deleted, while
hardware statistics keep both the flow and conntrack entry alive.

Validate both cached XFRM destinations from the periodic flowtable garbage
collector.  XFRM marks a deleted state dead before dropping its database
reference, so xfrm_dst_check() rejects the bundle and the normal hardware
delete path releases provider, state and destination references in order.

Assisted-by: Codex:GPT-5.6-sol
Signed-off-by: Yanghan Ye <yyh94306@gmail.com>
---
--- a/net/netfilter/nf_flow_table_core.c
+++ b/net/netfilter/nf_flow_table_core.c
@@ -452,6 +452,24 @@ static bool nf_flow_custom_gc(struct nf_f
 	return flow_table->type->gc && flow_table->type->gc(flow);
 }
 
+static bool nf_flow_xfrm_dst_valid(const struct flow_offload *flow)
+{
+	int dir;
+
+	for (dir = 0; dir < FLOW_OFFLOAD_DIR_MAX; dir++) {
+		const struct flow_offload_tuple *tuple;
+
+		tuple = &flow->tuplehash[dir].tuple;
+		if (tuple->xmit_type != FLOW_OFFLOAD_XMIT_XFRM)
+			continue;
+		if (!tuple->dst_cache ||
+		    !dst_check(tuple->dst_cache, tuple->dst_cookie))
+			return false;
+	}
+
+	return true;
+}
+
 /**
  * nf_flow_table_tcp_timeout() - new timeout of offloaded tcp entry
  * @ct:		Flowtable offloaded tcp ct
@@ -561,6 +579,7 @@ static void nf_flow_offload_gc_step(struc
 
 	if (nf_flow_has_expired(flow) ||
 	    nf_ct_is_dying(flow->ct) ||
+	    !nf_flow_xfrm_dst_valid(flow) ||
 	    nf_flow_custom_gc(flow_table, flow)) {
 		flow_offload_teardown(flow);
 		teardown = true;
